      <definitions><definition id="oval:mil.disa.stig.windows2025:def:278170" version="1" class="compliance">
          <metadata>
            <title>WN25-DC-000390 - The Windows Server 2025 "Deny log on as a service" user right must be configured to include no accounts or groups (blank) on domain controllers.</title>
            <affected family="windows">
              <platform>Microsoft Windows Server 2025</platform>
            </affected>
            <description>Inappropriately granting user rights provides system, administrative, and other high-level capabilities.

  The "Deny log on as a service" user right defines accounts that are denied logon as a service.

  Incorrect configurations could prevent services from starting and result in a denial of service.</description>
          </metadata>
